    "inventory_result": "Exactly these two raw-source rows differ from dc00;615 other inventory rows and the complete617 path set are equal. Both changed bodies match the freeze. The diff reconstructs exactly from the pinned public dc00 image copy. No other scientific/resource configuration change is proposed. I did not broadly reread/rehash615 unchanged bodies.",
    "production_change": "Both scalar preparePpoInEnvironment and device preparePpoOnDeviceWithEnvironment iteration steps add bang strictness to the existing actorStepsAfter, transitionsAfter and stat bindings. Their expressions are unchanged. The same rollout collection, advantages/standardisation, triples, optimizer/device calls, counters, generator/state threading and stats append remain in the same logical order. No sampling, update count, minibatch, epoch, seed, initialization, reference, evaluation, quality-bar or cap change is introduced.",
    "mechanism": "A deferred transition counter closes over rolloutSteps; a deferred summary closes over episode returns; a deferred actor counter may close over previous/current parameter roots. Eagerly obtaining the existing Int/Integer results consumes those thunks before advancing. PpoIterationStat already has strict Int/Double fields, so forcing its constructor also consumes its existing mean/median/max/count calculations. This changes evaluation timing and object lifetime, without changing the arithmetic expressions or selecting a different result. For TRPO the unchanged actor comparison is evaluated earlier. No forced GC, dropped statistic, censored result, shortened work or memory-limit increase is added to production.",
    "behavioral_test": "The new four-iteration/two-slot test instruments the actual pure-reference device seam. It identifies the first rollout call after an optimizer pass, triggers GC, checks a previous parameter root only through a weak pointer, and requires three boundaries and four result statistics. The actual old compiled library fails the expected lifetime assertion, while the current library passes the complete12-case group. This is useful behavioral regression evidence rather than merely checking the new syntax.",
    "limits": "Strictness can expose a bottom/exception earlier; it does not justify accepting an incomplete or invalid run. Static unchanged expressions plus the paired fixtures support numerical invariance for intended completed finite computations, not a universal bitwise theorem for every variant/backend/configuration. The paired device probe exercises VariantPPO on a synthetic pure-reference MlpDevice seam, not real oneDNN/Metal/CUDA training. The scalar probe supplies output equality only. Full result-statistic list retention and within-iteration peaks remain; no globally constant-space or product memory-fit claim is made."
  },
